        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ef058314-229b-5a02-b4fe-8fda3ad8912f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles White Whittlesey\n- Roles: United States Army officer, Medal of Honor recipient\n- Military Units: Lost Battalion\n- Events: Meuse-Argonne Offensive, World War I, final Allied offensive, Battle of the Argonne Forest\n- Places: Western Front\n\nFacts:\n- Charles White Whittlesey was born on January 20, 1884, and was presumed dead on November 26, 1921.\n- Charles White Whittlesey was a United States Army officer and an American Medal of Honor recipient.\n- In October 1918, during the final stages of World War I, Charles White Whittlesey led the Lost Battalion in the Meuse-Argonne Offensive.\n- The Meuse-Argonne Offensive was also known as the Maas-Argonne Offensive and the Battle of the Argonne Forest.\n- The Meuse-Argonne Offensive was a major part of the final Allied offensive of World War I that stretched along the entire Western Front.",
